# 7. Database Requirements

The project will use PostgreSQL for persistent storage.

The conceptual data model is:

```text
Customer
   |
   +------< Purchase
   |
   +------< Email
              |
              | 1 : 1
              v
            Ticket
              |
              +------ AI Analysis
              |
              +------ AI Response
```

### Customer

Stores customer information.

Expected fields:

* id
* name
* email
* address
* created_at

Customer email should be unique.

---

### Purchase

Stores customer purchase information.

Expected fields:

* id
* customer_id
* product_name
* amount
* purchased_at

Relationship:

```text
One Customer
      |
      +---- Many Purchases
```

---

### Email

Stores the original customer email.

Expected fields:

* id
* from
* customer_id
* subject
* body
* received_at

`customer_id` may be null when the sender is not found.

---

### Ticket

Represents the support ticket created for an email.

Expected fields:

* id
* email_id
* customer_id
* subject
* category
* status
* created_at
* updated_at

Each email creates exactly one ticket in the MVP.

---

### AI Analysis

Stores the AI analysis associated with the ticket.

Expected fields:

* id
* ticket_id
* sentiment
* priority
* category
* confidence
* created_at

A single confidence value will be used in the MVP rather than maintaining multiple confidence fields.

---

### AI Response

Stores the generated response and handling decision.

Expected fields:

* id
* ticket_id
* response_text
* decision
* created_at

Possible decisions:

```text
AUTO_REPLY
ESCALATE
```

